WEBVTT

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:31.288
so that the cells
reproduce more efficiently

00:02:31.329 --> 00:02:33.371
and more cells survive.

00:02:33.413 --> 00:02:36.246
But research shows that progenitor 
cells from these areas

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:38.913
can actually migrate to places
where injury has occurred

00:02:38.954 --> 00:02:42.579
and give rise to new neurons there.

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:45.413
And another promising possible approach

00:02:45.454 --> 00:02:48.038
is to transplant healthy
human neural stem cells,

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:51.496
which are cultured in a laboratory,
to injured tissue,

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.746
like we can do with skin.

00:02:54.413 --> 00:02:56.329
Scientists are currently experimenting

00:02:56.371 --> 00:03:00.996
to determine whether transplanted
donor cells can divide, differentiate